{
  "description": "Replacement of existing single glazed timber framed windows to front elevation with double glazed timber framed sash windows and \nreplacement of the timber framed single glazed windows on the flank and rear elevation with genesis heritage PVCU windows to match the existing size, dimension and function. \n\nThe existing windows will be replaced with a new window of the same design e.g. casement for casement.\n\nThis planning application is a resubmission of the previously submitted proposal, incorporating the additional details and amendments requested by the Planning Officer. The revised proposal includes the introduction of a transom bar together with concealed trickle vents to the windows. The trickle vents have been carefully integrated within the window design and positioned so that they are not visible from street level, thereby minimising their visual impact and ensuring that the appearance and character of the building is maintained. This design is the most efficient way to introduce passive ventilation without causing visual changes to original windows as reference to the conservation area.\n\nThese amendments have been incorporated in response to the Planning Officer’s comments and to ensure that the proposed works satisfy the relevant Building Regulations requirements while also addressing the planning and heritage considerations associated with the property. The revised details do not materially alter the overall design intent of the proposal and are intended to provide the necessary ventilation and technical requirements whilst preserving the architectural character and visual appearance of the building.\n\nWe have been in contact with planning officer Mark Price who has agreed to this proposal when consulted via email. ",
